IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa6-vacancy`
IMPORT `coa6-dual-capacity`

-- coa6-tests-vacancy-and-dual-capacity.l4: tests of coa6-vacancy.l4 (s 274) and coa6-dual-capacity.l4 (s 280).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section (lines 3617-3620 and 3715-3716 of ukpga-2006-46.txt) before the
-- encoding was run, and is written beside its assertion.

§ `Tests: ss 274 and 280`

-- ---- s 274: the case the section covers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- arguments: the office is vacant?, there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting?
#ASSERT `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 274(a) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- arguments: vacant?, no secretary capable?, thing required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary?, the person is an
-- assistant or deputy secretary?
#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a grant: the person is not an assistant or deputy secretary, so the text does not answer (NOTHING, not FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the thing is not one the secretary was to do or receive
#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the office is not vacant and a secretary is capable of acting
#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or ..." is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 274(b) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- arguments: vacant?, no secretary capable?, thing required or authorised?, no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable?,
-- the person is authorised generally or specifically by the directors?
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting stands first
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the person is not authorised by the directors
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the thing is not one the secretary was to do or receive
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the case the section covers does not arise
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or ..." is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE
-- both gates fail (no vacancy, and an assistant or deputy secretary is capable of acting): the "Where" decides, JUST FALSE (the "if" gate is NOTHING only inside the "Where")
#ASSERT `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 280: a person acting in dual capacity -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "A provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company is not satisfied by
-- its being done by or to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary."
-- arguments: the provision requires or authorises a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary?, the thing is done by
-- or to the same person?, that person acts both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary?
#ASSERT `s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the thing was done by two different people (a director, and separately the secretary): s 280 says nothing of that case
#ASSERT `s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- one person did it but not in both capacities
#ASSERT `s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a provision that does not ask for both a director and the secretary
#ASSERT `s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
